{"desk_safe_2_min":[
"Open a draft message or scratch doc and type one neutral sentence about the current task, then re-read it twice as if you’re editing for clarity.",
"Silently label the next three concrete steps on your screen (e.g., “open ticket / check logs / reply”), then do only the first step.",
"Plant both feet, keep your hands on mouse/keyboard, and shift your attention to the contact points (feet-floor, hands-keys) while you keep working normally."
],
"containment_10_min":[
"Take your phone/notepad to the bathroom, lock a stall, and sit there doing nothing but reading a harmless page (news/weather) until the timer is up.",
"Walk to the water station, refill, and stand there while you “review” one ticket on your phone (no replying), then return.",
"Go to the printer/supply area with a paper in hand, pretend to look for something, and spend the time quietly scanning one backlog list without responding."
]}
